  "result": "Fixed. The bug was a reversed comparison in `shop/storage.py:17`.\n\n**Root cause:** `save_order` reads the existing rows, removes any old copy of this order, appends the new row and writes the file back. But the filter was `r[\"id\"] == order.id`, which kept only the old copy of the order being saved and dropped every other order. So each save overwrote the file with just one order. Changing it to `!=` keeps all other orders and replaces only the one being saved.\n\n**Verification:**\n- **Repro script:** saving orders for customers `a` and `b` and then re-saving a third order after `move('paid')` now loads all three, with the third in state `paid` and no duplicate.\n- **Tests:** pytest isn't installed, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest`. All 6 tests pass. None of them cover `Store`, so the suite never caught this bug and won't catch it coming back.\n\nWant me to add a regression test for `Store.save_order` in `tests/`?",
